ecture’s final bound-system calculation without repeating the selected orbital-dynamics material."}],"coverage_gaps":["No playlist entry directly treats two comparable masses orbiting a common center of mass, derives T² = 4π²d³/[G(M+m)], or emphasizes that the mutual separation differs from either body’s orbital radius.","No entry directly covers three equal masses rotating at the vertices of an equilateral triangle, including the symmetry result Fnet = √3Gm²/L², R = L/√3, and v = √(Gm/L).","The energy selection is only a general match: no listed video explicitly covers U = −Gm₁m₂/r with zero at infinity, counting each unique gravitational pair once, or interpreting negative total energy as gravitational binding."]}
